content.text:
Now ai.js updateKeepers. We need to replace the incoming block.

Current:
```
const incoming = !game.owner && towardGoal > 12 && ballToGoal < 16;
if (incoming && !keeper.dive.active) {
  const pred = predictX(game, goalZ);
  const delta = pred - keeper.pos.x;
  if (Math.abs(delta) > 0.32) {
    keeper.setDive(Math.sign(delta) || 1);
    keeper.diveTargetX = clamp(pred, ...);
    keeper.diveSpeed = 11.5 * game.difficulty.keeperSpeed;
    keeper.aiSprint = false;
  }
}
```
Replace with reaction plan:
```
const incoming = !game.owner && towardGoal > 11 && ballToGoal < 17;
if (!incoming) {
  keeper.incoming = false;
  keeper.reactTimer = 0;
  keeper.divePlan = null;
} else if (!keeper.dive.active) {
  if (!keeper.incoming) {
    keeper.incoming = true;
    keeper.reactTimer = game.difficulty.keeperReaction ?? 0.16;
    keeper.divePlan = null;
  }
  keeper.reactTimer = Math.max(0, keeper.reactTimer - dt);
  if (keeper.reactTimer <= 0 && !keeper.divePlan) {
    const spread = game.difficulty.keeperError ?? 0.6;
    const err = (Math.random() * 2 - 1) * spread * clamp(ballToGoal / 16, 0.45, 1.25);
    keeper.divePlan = clamp(predictX(game, goalZ) + err, -goalWidth/2+0.2, goalWidth/2-0.2);
  }
  if (keeper.divePlan != null) {
    const delta = keeper.divePlan - keeper.pos.x;
    if (Math.abs(delta) > 0.3) {
      keeper.setDive(Math.sign(delta)||1);
      keeper.diveTargetX = keeper.divePlan;
      keeper.diveSpeed = game.difficulty.keeperDiveSpeed ?? 8.5;
      keeper.aiSprint = false;
    }
  }
}
```
But if the keeper is already at divePlan (delta small), it won't dive; resolveKeeperBall may catch. Good. If the keeper dives, `divePlan` remains; next frame `keeper.dive.active` true, skip. After dive ends (0.75s), if incoming still, it will start a new dive? `keeper.incoming` true, `reactTimer` 0, `divePlan` remains. It would dive again toward the same plan if delta > 0.3. Fine, but after 0.75s the ball likely passed. Could reset `divePlan` when dive ends; not necessary.

Also reset `keeper.incoming` during kickoff/reset? `resetForKickoff` doesn't reset these; but incoming becomes false next update when ball not incoming. Fine. On kickoff, owner exists so incoming false; resets.

Also the keeper's `diveSpeed` used in `updateKeepers` movement block. Fine.

Update reach line:
```
const reach = (1.0 + (keeper.dive.active ? 0.55 : 0)) * game.difficulty.keeperReach;
```
Maybe base 1.0 is a bit small for standing saves but okay; keepers have hands. Use 1.05. For pro dive 1.6. Let's use `(1.05 + (dive?0.5:0))`. Pro standing 1.05, dive 1.55. Good.

Also in the "incoming" detection, use `ballToGoal < 17` and `towardGoal > 11`.

Let's patch.

