Now updateDribble. Currently:
```
let tx = o.pos.x + fx*offset + o.vel.x*0.035;
let tz = o.pos.z + fz*offset + o.vel.z*0.035;
tx += Math.cos(o.runPhase)*0.045;
tz -= Math.sin(o.runPhase)*0.045;
```
Add side offset 0.3:
```
let tx = ... + Math.cos(o.facing)*0.3 + Math.cos(o.runPhase)*0.045;
let tz = ... - Math.sin(o.facing)*0.3 - Math.sin(o.runPhase)*0.045;
```
Wait the side offset for facing 0 should be +x 0.3. cos(0)=1, -sin(0)=0. Good. For facing π/2 (facing +x), side +x? The right side of a player facing +x is -z (cos(π/2)=0, -sin(π/2)=-1). So tz -0.3. Good.

Let's patch.

